    {
      "id": 473950,
      "username": "Maveez",
      "name": "Maveez MH",
      "created_at": "2025-07-15T10:48:29.768Z",
      "cooked": "<p>better use manual method until its fixed. erpnext is using mixed method of depreciation where initially its updating higher depreciation values and later switching to straight line method (if you have monthly depreciation)</p>\n<p>Since ERPNext applies the <strong>double declining rate</strong> on the <strong>opening book value for the year</strong>, then spreads it monthly.</p>\n<p>Switch to a longer depreciation period, For very short lives, DDB behaves almost like straight line. Extending life to 2 years or more makes the declining effect clearer.</p>\n<p>refer to same asset of 200K depreciated across multiple years</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/8/7/87d4eacf421ebde16ccbc82235c88798f55272bd.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/87d4eacf421ebde16ccbc82235c88798f55272bd\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/7/87d4eacf421ebde16ccbc82235c88798f55272bd_2_690x333.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"jnCD9IKQKTzHUhDdQefpVOGzbiJ\" width=\"690\" height=\"333\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/7/87d4eacf421ebde16ccbc82235c88798f55272bd_2_690x333.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/7/87d4eacf421ebde16ccbc82235c88798f55272bd_2_1035x499.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/8/7/87d4eacf421ebde16ccbc82235c88798f55272bd_2_1380x666.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"FBFBFB\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1627×787 43.9 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
